      "desc:8": "Autocrafting jobs live in a Crafting CPU: a square multiblock of Crafting Units. Storage units (1k to 64k) provide the bytes a job occupies; co-processing units add parallel assemblers to a job. One CPU multiblock runs one job, on one channel, however big it is.\n\nShape it from a frame and two 1k crafting storages; the cats add accelerator units so your first jobs run wide.\n\nRule of thumb: many small CPUs beat one giant one — jobs queue badly on big blocks.",
